<span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Local Areas</span>
<h1>Ha Dong by Motorbike: Motorbike Day-Ride Ideas in Hanoi</h1>
<p>Ha Dong rewards the rider who plans days rather than routes, because the district&rsquo;s riding map is a hybrid of an old town&rsquo;s amble, corridors that carry the southwest&rsquo;s real flow, the silk quarter at Van Phuc and the open edges at the district&rsquo;s back. A day built here has a shape before it has streets, a morning&rsquo;s errand layer, a loose middle for the pleasure lines, and an evening that belongs to the lanes, and this page lays out the shapes that work, flexibly, around landmarks and rider comfort rather than fixed promises. No times are invented, because the day&rsquo;s clock belongs to the flow.</p>
<p>The rental counter is at Motorbike Rental - Nguyen Tu, 112 Nguyen Van Cu in Long Bien, across the Red River, so the day-ride menu starts from a base the stay plans around. Start at the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/">Old Quarter motorbike rental</a> hub, see the machines and the verified prices at the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> guide, browse the wider <a href="/motorbike-guides/">motorbike guides</a>, and for the neighbouring days read the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/thanh-xuan-day-ride-ideas/">Thanh Xuan day-ride ideas</a> page and the <a href="/motorbike-rental-hanoi-old-quarter/hoang-mai-rental-planning/">Hoang Mai rental planning</a> guide, the corridor&rsquo;s nearer and southern neighbours.</p>
<nav class="toc">
<ol>
<li><a href="#sec-1">Choosing the shape of the day</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-2">The market and old town idea</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-3">The silk quarter morning idea</a></li>
<li><a href="#sec-4">The southwestern edges idea</a></li>
